# Local hardware-probe scratch.  _probe/ holds the captured AT transcripts used
# while reverse-engineering the module on real hardware, plus verbatim copies of
# QModem's own vendor scripts that were pulled off the test router.  It stays
# out of the published tree on purpose: the transcripts contain real device
# identifiers (IMEI, serial number) and the vendor scripts are upstream's work,
# not ours.  The findings that matter are written up in docs/HARDWARE-PROBE.md.
_probe/
_probe-*/

# Build products
*.o
*.so
*.ipk
*.apk
fm160d/fm160d
fm160d/src/fm160d
at-daemon/src/ubus-at-daemon

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# tools/i18n/check.py proves its orphan scan can fail by appending a planted
# msgid to a copy of the po.  That copy is a test fixture, not a translation.
*.po.mut

# Verification scratch.  _tmp/ holds the po2lmo built by
# tools/i18n/build-po2lmo.sh and the .lmo compiled from the shipped .po; both
# are products of a checkout, not sources.  The caches belong to zig.
_tmp/
tools/cccheck/.zigcache/
tools/cccheck/out/
